## Alerts

**The main screen had all the information, but it was hard to read and scan**

{% block title="Eight alerts squeezed on one screen" %}
Eight alerts were squeezed on one screen, with titles of 12 to 16 words in a tiny column and small dates and distances fighting for attention. The engineers' idea was to show as much as possible without scrolling, so the question became: see everything at once, or read each alert easily? My first thought was "where should I be looking?" There was no way to search by place either, and no profile or way to reach terms, FAQs or info about the app, just a settings icon at the top right.
{% /block %}

{% figure src="projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/inso-app-old-alerts-screen.jpg" frame="before" size="text" alt="The old alerts list, annotated: inconsistent typography, low spacing between items, and location, distance and time not prioritised." caption="Alerts screen before redesign, showing density and unclear hierarchy" /%}

{% tablebox label="table" %}
| Alerts list, former design | Redesign approach |
|---|---|
| Five type styles competed in a 70px row: bold all caps titles, small caps locations, all caps dates, tiny right-aligned distance and time | One title style in sentence case, and a clear secondary level for the rest |
| Location, the thing people scan for, was the smallest element, under a four-line title | Location first, then a short title, then time |
| Alerts were separated by a hairline with almost no padding, so rows merged | More space and a clearer boundary between rows |
| No search, no filter and no account area, just an unlabelled orange circle and a settings icon | Search at the top, a simpler filter, and an entry for the profile, terms and help |
| Every alert had the same warning icon, with no cue for new or unseen alerts and no way to save | A marker for unseen alerts, a Recent Alerts block, and a save button on each alert |
{% /tablebox %}

{% cut note="Repeats the table. Keep the scrolling trade-off as one line under it?" /%}

{% block title="Built for scanning, not for seeing everything" %}
Scanning came first, with more space and a clear order of location, title and time. Then search at the top, a simpler filter and a list/map toggle. Fewer alerts per screen does mean more scrolling, but with search and filters you can go straight to a place, so it matters much less. The map-and-listings idea came from apps like Airbnb, and country office colleagues found it familiar straight away.
{% /block %}

{% cut end=true /%}

{% cut note="Trim from 12 to 6 slides." /%}

{% sequence images="projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/01-alerts_first_view.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/02-alerts_list_instruct_01.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/03-alerts_search_typing.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/04-alerts_search_results.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/05-alerts_list_instruct_02.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/06-alerts_filter_off.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/07-alerts_filter_date_picker.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/08-alerts_filtered.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/09-alerts_list_instruct_03.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/10-map_explore_loading.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/11-map_explore_loaded.jpg, projects/mitigating-risk-with-location-based-alerts/simple/alerts-and-filters/12-map_explore_alert-selected.jpg" landscape=true frame="after" alts="The new alerts list: location first, then a short title, then time.|In-app guide, 1 of 3: search anything in alerts.|Typing a search.|Search results for Ukraine.|In-app guide, 2 of 3: filter alerts by date.|The filter: programmes and regions, and a date range.|The date picker, with quick options like last week.|The list, filtered.|In-app guide, 3 of 3: explore alerts in a map view.|The map opens in Explore mode.|The map with the alerts in the area.|An alert opened on the map." caption="The new alerts list: built for scanning, with search at the top, a simpler filter and a list/map toggle." /%}

{% cut end=true /%}

